        "id": "ch2_2-2",
        "text": "I %s : Means we\u2019re inserting a string (text) in this position\nI\nI %d : Means we\u2019re adding a decimal (number) in this position\nI\nI \\n : Means that we want to go to a new line when the print is finished\nAlso, take note that we are using double quotes instead of single quotes.\nDouble quotes will allow us to be more flexible with string manipulation than\nthe single quotes. So, most of the time, we can use the double quotes for printf\n(we rarely need to use the single quotes).\nTo format a string using the printf command, you can use the following\npatterns:\nI\nI %s : String (texts)\nI\nI %d : Decimal (numbers)\nI\nI %f : Floating-point (including signed numbers)\nI\nI %x : Hexadecimal\nI\nI \\n : New line\nI\nI \\r : Carriage return\nI\nI \\t : Horizontal tab",
